# Moby-Dick oracle batch 4 (public domain, Melville d. 1891).
# Hand-tagged UPOS, UD tokenization (punctuation split, contractions
# split UD-style [`cannot`→`can`+`not`, `'ll` split], ASCII
# apostrophes), EWT-side conventions per CANONICAL.md (predicative
# participles ADJ, reduced relatives VERB, temporal-when ADV,
# existentials There/PRON + VERB, `as`-clauses SCONJ,
# possessive-`have`/`had` VERB, `at all` ADP+DET 27:0, `other` ADJ,
# `such` ADJ, `all/those` DET, `one` PRON, particles ADP).
# Sentences from chapters 3 and 27-30 — disjoint from the ch.1-2
# prose eval and batches 01 (ch.4-6), 02 (ch.5-6), 03 (ch.7-26).
# Boundary-BALANCED by design (the batch-03 lesson): every passive
# `be`+VBN pairs AUX-be with VERB-participle (counter-observing the
# VERB→AUX drift), reduced relatives stay VERB, and NO new
# predicative-ADJ participles are added (that boundary is genuinely
# ambiguous 138:22 in EWT — J2 deferred, unteachable by data).
# Contested calls (EWT train counts): `as`-clause SCONJ (as+PRON
# 78:0); `after`+gerund SCONJ (clausal); `at all` ADP+DET 27:0;
# `other` ADJ 268:1; `thy` PRON 3:0; `bound` untouched (not here);
# `tost`/`fain` ADJ (predicative, zero-observation, test-safe);
# generic-plural `Senators`/`Judges` NOUN; subjunctive `pluck`
# VERB (base form); `but`-except CCONJ; `above` ADV (measure use).
